GRAYBOX 0
# FPS-GRAYBOX-0: the tactical graybox. Its walls and floor are tactical.layout, which the design compiler produced
# from tactical.design. This file adds only what the design language does not say: heights, cover, spawns, the
# objective, targets, probes and routes, each on floor cells. Coordinates are cells, x across and z down; a cell is
# `cell` metres. The map is point-symmetric about the plaza's centre.
name tactical
layout tactical.layout
cell 2
wall 4

# spawn regions: base A in the west, base B in the east; yaw in degrees, 0 north (-z), 90 east (+x)
spawn A 3,15 90
spawn B 44,16 270

# the central engagement: a raised platform in the plaza, a step on every side, the objective on top
height 21,12 26,19 0.5
height 22,13 25,18 1.0
objective 22,14 25,17
# tall pillars at the plaza's corners break the long sightlines across it
cover 20,11 20,11 2.6
cover 27,11 27,11 2.6
cover 20,20 20,20 2.6
cover 27,20 27,20 2.6

# the mid lane: low cover, 1 m, that a jump mounts
cover 12,14 12,14 1.0
cover 12,17 12,17 1.0
cover 16,15 16,16 1.0
cover 31,15 31,16 1.0
cover 35,14 35,14 1.0
cover 35,17 35,17 1.0

# the side lanes: crates and pillars, the south lane the north lane turned about the centre
cover 11,4 11,5 1.0
cover 36,26 36,27 1.0
cover 17,5 17,5 2.6
cover 30,26 30,26 2.6
cover 21,4 21,4 1.0
cover 26,27 26,27 1.0
cover 28,6 28,6 1.0
cover 19,25 19,25 1.0
cover 33,4 34,4 1.0
cover 13,27 14,27 1.0
cover 38,5 38,5 2.6
cover 9,26 9,26 2.6

# at the bases' exits
cover 8,12 8,12 1.0
cover 39,19 39,19 1.0

# targets
target 10,16
target 37,15
target 24,11
target 23,20
target 26,4
target 21,27

# probes: cells that must block, and cells that must stay open
probe wall 1,15
probe wall 23,2
probe wall 9,10
probe open 23,8
probe open 24,23
probe open 6,8
probe open 41,24

# the three routes from base A to base B
route north 3,15 6,4 41,4 44,16
route mid 3,15 20,15 23,15 27,16 44,16
route south 3,15 6,27 41,27 44,16
